This Java code uses the Jsoup library to parse HTML and extract the text content of all elements that have a class named "text". It then prints out this extracted text.

Please note that if there are no child nodes (like text, comments, etc.) in the selected elements, `Jsoup.parse(html).select(".text")` will return an empty Jsoup Document object. In such cases, calling `.body().outerHtml()` on this document will also return an empty string.

Also, note that the class "text" is not a standard HTML class, but rather a class defined by your own CSS styling. If you want to extract text from all elements with a specific ID or attribute, you should use that instead of ".text".
